cases.prompt:
Review this one function under its stated contract: both intervals are nonempty integer half-open ranges, with endpoints in -32..32. There is one boundary defect. Return JSON {"findings":[{"line":integer,"a":[start,end],"b":[start,end],"actual":boolean,"expected":boolean}]}. Give one concrete counterexample, identify the faulty source line, and add no unverified findings.
def overlaps(a, b):
    """Nonempty integer half-open intervals, with endpoints in -32..32."""
    return max(a[0], b[0]) <= min(a[1], b[1])

