cases.prompt:
Design four to eight distinct parameter cases for this run-length encoder. Return JSON {"tests":[{"input":string,"expected":[[one_character,positive_count],...]}]}. Include empty input, adjacent repeats, equal characters separated by another run, and Unicode. Every expected result must reconstruct the input and have distinct adjacent run labels. The cases must detect mutants that merge nonadjacent equal characters or drop the final run. Input length is at most 128 characters. Return data only.
def rle(text):
    runs = []
    for char in text:
        if runs and runs[-1][0] == char:
            runs[-1][1] += 1
        else:
            runs.append([char, 1])
    return runs

